From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 18:57:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0206 -- #31 v1.0.8 audio-delivery: Organya pre-render
 producer (ship)

Ship form of the head-to-head winner (A-minimal pre-render). DEFAULT-ON;
killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_ORG_PRERENDER=0 reverts to the live synth-on-
demand producer. The org loop [0..loop_end] is synthesized to a static mono
PCM buffer; the per-frame producer is then a memcpy-from-static. Offloading
the synth from the playback pull is what lets the 486 reach real-time organya
tempo (g2k-proven ~19 fps real-time vs the live-synth ~47%-tempo wall).

TRIGGER POLICY (freeze-avoidance, team-lead-directed): the at-start render is
a ~10-14 s synth pass on the 486. At a stage entry that blends with the load
pause; a MID-GAMEPLAY <CMU (boss/event, no preceding load) must NOT freeze.
So the render only runs inside the POST-LOAD WINDOW (a flag armed at
load_stage, consumed by the first song-start = the stage-entry song); a later
mid-gameplay <CMU that is not a cache hit (patch 0208) falls back to LIVE
SYNTH (no freeze, ~47%). Patch 0209 caches the live-played song at the next
load so a re-encounter is real-time. Net: no mid-gameplay freeze ever;
boss song slow-not-frozen first encounter, real-time after.

Engages only when organya is the active backend (production default OPL3/WB
never pre-renders). Bounded PCM (~1.3 MB/60s @ 11025 mono). Volume/fade at
read time so fades/pause work. Exposes org_prerender_buffer_ready() for the
0207 pump gate. Q-SAFE oversample opt-in default-OFF. Renderer factored
(_org_render_song) for reuse by the 0209 deferred cache. map.cpp arms the
window in the load_stage phase guard. Diag-free ship form of experiment 0204.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
